  </ul>

  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-[#202020] dark:text-[#fcfcfc] mb-4 mt-8">
    How to Report Phishing Emails
  </h2>

  <p class="text-base text-[#575757] dark:text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
    Reporting phishing attacks helps protect millions of other internet users by triggering automated global blocklists:
  </p>

  <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-base text-[#575757] dark:text-zinc-300 mb-4">
    <li><strong>Inside your email client:</strong> Click the three dots menu and select <em>"Report Phishing"</em> (or <em>"Report Junk"</em>).</li>
    <li><strong>To the Anti-Phishing Working Group (APWG):</strong> Forward the phishing email as an attachment to <code>reportphishing@apwg.org</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>To the US Federal Trade Commission (FTC):</strong> Forward suspicious emails to <code>reportphishing@ftc.gov</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>To the spoofed organization:</strong> Forward fraudulent emails mimicking brands to their dedicated abuse lines (e.g., <code>phishing@paypal.com</code> or <code>reportphishing@apple.com</code>).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-[#202020] dark:text-[#fcfcfc] mb-4 mt-8">
    Conclusion: Stay Vigilant, Stay Private
  </h2>

  <p class="text-base text-[#575757] dark:text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
    In an era of sophisticated social engineering, healthy skepticism is your strongest security asset. Always inspect sender domains, never allow artificial urgency to dictate your actions, and compartmentalize your online identity by using <a href="/" class="text-[#ea2804] hover:underline">TempoEmails</a> for untrusted signups and verification codes.
  </p>

